# Sound, as an iPhone's Settings panel has it: Send Audio (the other Mac's, for every device) starts off
# on a test host and is turned on from the sidebar; the Desktop then streams the test tone, decoded here
# (a harness run plays nothing); Mute on This Mac stops it here alone, and Send Audio stays on.
wait apps 30
expect sound.sendAudio == off
expect sound.muted == false
snap sound-off.png
click 180 513
wait sendaudio 5
expect sound.sendAudio == on
click 75 242
wait sound 15
expect sound.frames > 0
snap sound-on.png
click 180 539
expect sound.muted == true
expect sound.frames == 0
expect sound.sendAudio == on
wait stream 1
expect sound.frames == 0
click 180 539
wait sound 10
expect sound.muted == false
expect sound.frames > 0
